# <%= current_page.data.title %>

When you create a new component (application, data store, or shared infrastructure), follow this workflow.

## Step 1: Choose your application type first

If you are creating an application service, start with the guidance for your runtime:

- [Java golden path](https://backstage.platform.hmcts.net/docs/default/component/golden-path-java)
- [Node.js golden path](https://backstage.platform.hmcts.net/docs/default/component/golden-path-nodejs)
- [Python services](python.html)

After completing runtime-specific setup, return to this page and continue with the common steps below.

If you are creating infrastructure-only components, skip this step and go straight to the common workflow.

## Step 2: Common workflow for all components

1. [Create a new GitHub repository](github-repo.html)
2. [Add the repository to Jenkins](jenkins-repository.html)
3. [Add a Helm chart](helm-chart.html) for deployable services
4. [Add infrastructure as code](infrastructure-as-code.html) where infrastructure is required
5. [Configure GitOps with Flux](gitops-flux.html#application-config-in-flux)
6. [Set up secrets management](secrets-management.html)
7. For service components, complete [Path-to-live](../path-to-live/) setup, including non-production requirements
8. Use [feature flags](feature-flags.html) to safely release changes

